\section*{Key relations (hand-transcribed from the PDF)}

The paper is predominantly experimental (CD-ARPES / SARPES) + DFT; it states
few numbered display equations. The physically load-bearing relations are:

\paragraph{Spin and orbital magnetic moments (Sec. I).}
\[ \vec{m}_S = -\,g_S\,\frac{e}{2m_e}\,\vec{S}, \qquad g_S \approx 2, \tag{1} \]
\[ \vec{m}_L = -\,g_L\,\frac{e}{2m_e}\,\vec{L}, \qquad g_L = 1. \tag{2} \]

\paragraph{Circular-dichroism ARPES observable (Sec. II), OAM proxy.}
\[ I_{\mathrm{CD}}(\vec{k}) \;=\; I_{\mathrm{RCP}}(\vec{k}) - I_{\mathrm{LCP}}(\vec{k})
   \;\propto\; \vec{L}(\vec{k})\cdot \hat{\vec{q}}_{\mathrm{photon}}, \tag{3} \]
i.e. CD is sensitive to the OAM component along the light propagation direction;
with the plane of incidence in $xz$ and chain axis $\parallel x$, CD probes
$L_x$ (and in principle $L_z$).

\paragraph{p-wave (odd-parity) OAM texture — the headline (Sec. III).}
\[ L_x(+k_x) = +|L_x|, \qquad L_x(-k_x) = -|L_x|
   \quad\Longrightarrow\quad L_x(-k_x) = -\,L_x(k_x). \tag{4} \]
$L_x$ is (largely) independent of $k_y$; $L_y$ weak; $L_z$ absent along $k_y=0$.

\paragraph{Enantiomer / mirror relations ($\vec{k}$ polar, $\vec{L}$ axial) (Sec. II).}
Under $M_x$ ($k_x\to-k_x$): $L_x,k_y$ unchanged, so it maps enantiomer A onto B:
\[ L_x^{B}(-k_x,\,k_y) = L_x^{A}(k_x,\,k_y). \tag{5} \]
Under $M_y$ ($k_y\to-k_y$): $k_x$ unchanged, $L_x\to-L_x$ (and $k_y\to-k_y$):
\[ L_x^{B}(k_x,\,-k_y) = -\,L_x^{A}(k_x,\,k_y). \tag{6} \]
Consequently the two enantiomers carry globally opposite $L_x$ textures:
\[ L_x^{B}(\vec{k}) = -\,L_x^{A}(\vec{k}). \tag{7} \]
($L_z$ would flip sign under BOTH $M_x$ and $M_y$, incompatible with the data —
hence the observed CD reflects $L_x$, not $L_z$.)

\paragraph{OAM dominates SAM at low energy (Sec. IV).}
Weak SOC $\xi\,\vec{L}\cdot\vec{S}$ splits the band by $\Delta_{\mathrm{SOC}} < 5$ meV
$\ll k_B T_{300\mathrm{K}} \approx 25$ meV. The two split branches share the
same OAM sign but carry opposite SAM:
\[ L_x^{(1)}\approx L_x^{(2)}, \qquad S_x^{(1)} \approx -\,S_x^{(2)}
   \;\Longrightarrow\; \sum S_x \approx 0,\;\; \sum L_x \neq 0. \tag{8} \]

\section*{Model surrogate Hamiltonian built in this replication}

Minimal chiral $p$-orbital tight-binding model in the basis $(p_x,p_y,p_z)$,
$\chi=+1$ (enantiomer A) / $-1$ (enantiomer B); $L_a$ = $p$-orbital angular
momentum matrices, $(L_a)_{jk}=-i\,\varepsilon_{ajk}$:
\[ H(\vec{k}) = \varepsilon(\vec{k})\,\mathbb{1}_3 + \mathrm{diag}(\epsilon_{p_x},\epsilon_{p},\epsilon_{p}+\delta)
   + \chi A \sin k_x\, L_x + \chi B \sin k_x\, L_y + \chi C \sin k_y\, L_z, \tag{M1} \]
\[ \varepsilon(\vec{k}) = -2 t_x \cos k_x - 2 t_y \cos k_y. \tag{M2} \]
The chiral term $\chi A \sin k_x\,L_x$ is the $p$-wave OAM generator: it is odd
in $k_x$ (giving Eq. 4), lives in the $\{p_y,p_z\}$ "orbital-polarizer" doublet,
and flips sign with helicity $\chi$ (giving Eq. 7). $L_z$ operator on the
occupied Bloch states follows the expectation-over-states workflow of the
gobel2024 skyrmion OHE kernel (arXiv:2410.00820). With $C=0$, $L_z$ is absent.

OAM texture is read out as the expectation value over the lowest band:
\[ L_a(\vec{k}) = \langle \psi_0(\vec{k}) |\, L_a\, | \psi_0(\vec{k}) \rangle. \tag{M3} \]

